/* Embeds src/starfish.manifest into starfish.exe.

   Without it a MinGW build has no manifest, Windows falls back to pre-Windows-8
   compatibility behaviour, and WS_EX_LAYERED cannot be added to a child window:
   the hosted zones are then never composited by DWM (ADR-4, T-020).

   1  = CREATEPROCESS_MANIFEST_RESOURCE_ID
   24 = RT_MANIFEST */
1 24 "starfish.manifest"

/* The application icon: what Explorer, the taskbar and Alt-Tab show. Windows
   uses the first icon group in the resource table, so this is the one resource
   id that must stay low. The .ico carries nine frames (16 to 256 px) and this
   statement is toolchain-agnostic -- the keyword form needs no header, and the
   relative path resolves next to this file on both windres and rc.exe, exactly
   like the manifest above.

   Generated by tools/make_icon.py; regenerate rather than edit the .ico. */
1 ICON "starfish.ico"
